@startuml
!include ../_style.iuml
' C4 level 1 (system context), drawn with plain PlantUML (no remote includes, so it renders offline).
' Derived from README.md (overlay, candidate, interviewer and workplace modes, local-first, no telemetry),
' src-tauri/src/local_ai.rs (sidecar spawned locally), crates/openmeet-providers/src/factory.rs and
' anthropic.rs / openai.rs / ollama.rs (remote and local LLM providers), local-ai/room/__init__.py and
' room_server.py (interview room served from the interviewer's computer), local-ai/room/followups.py and
' room.js (Google Gemini in online mode, Google STUN for ICE), src-tauri/src/secrets.rs (OS keyring).
title C4 level 1: OpenMeet system context

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #F6F7FD
  BorderColor #4F5BD5
  RoundCorner 12
}

actor "Candidate\n(answers; uses the desktop overlay)" as Cand
actor "Interviewer\n(asks; uses the desktop app or the room)" as Iv
actor "Team member\n(workplace meetings: board, catch me up, minutes)" as Wp

rectangle "OpenMeet\n[software system]\nLocal-first meeting copilot: transcription,\nsuggestions, follow-ups, answer-integrity flag" as OM #E6E9FB

rectangle "Meeting app\n[external]\nZoom, Teams, Google Meet, Slack, Discord ...\n(audio and screen are read locally, never sent by the app)" as Meet #FFFFFF
rectangle "Local LLM server\n[external, on this computer]\nOllama (127.0.0.1:11434) or an\nOpenAI-compatible server" as OLLAMA #FFFFFF
rectangle "Remote LLM / transcription APIs\n[external, optional]\nOpenAI, Anthropic (only when chosen\nand local_only is off)" as Remote #FFFFFF
rectangle "Google Gemini\n[external, optional]\nonly in the interview room's\nonline follow-up mode" as Gemini #FFFFFF
rectangle "Google STUN\n[external]\nfinds a network route for the\nroom's video (no media passes)" as Stun #FFFFFF

Cand --> Meet : takes the call
Iv --> Meet : runs the meeting
Cand --> OM : sees suggestions in the overlay
Iv --> OM : sees follow-ups and integrity flags
Wp --> OM : sees the live board, catch-up and minutes
Iv ..> OM : hosts a browser interview room\n(room_server.py, local network)
OM --> Meet : captures system audio and\nscreen (Windows loopback, screen capture)
OM --> OLLAMA : suggestions, embeddings
OM ..> Remote : suggestions (if configured;\nkeys in the OS keyring)
OM ..> Gemini : room follow-ups (online mode)
OM ..> Stun : room connection only

note bottom of OM
  Nothing is sent to a project server: there is no
  telemetry. Remote providers receive only what the
  user's chosen provider needs, and local_only refuses them.
end note
@enduml
